         What this implies:                                                     
         - The root misconfiguration remains: Service named-target-service      
         declares targetPort: web, but the container port is 8765 with port name
         http-app. Because the targetPort is not a valid port name on the       
         container, traffic routed by the Service likely cannot reach the       
         application port.                                                      
         - Although the Pod itself is Ready and serving on 8765, traffic through
         the Service is not guaranteed to reach that port due to the port-name  
         mismatch.                                                              
                                                                                
